 #: kstars.kcfg:3127
 #, kde-format
 msgid ""
-"The pulse response test measures the mount's elastic response to guide "
-"pulses (harmonic drives). It adds about 20 minutes to the protocol and has "
-"not produced measurable results on rigs tested so far, so it is off by "
-"default."
+"Sends known pulses at the start of the protocol and measures the mount's "
+"step response to derive a base RA/DEC guiding gain for any mount type. The "
+"measured gain is applied and locked for the rest of the session, so the data "
+"that follows is collected under it; the current gain is kept unchanged if "
+"the responses do not pass the consistency checks. Adds roughly 20 minutes to "
+"the protocol. Enabled by default."
